  "number": "1.4.14",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Review the vocabulary in this lesson. Drag the vocabulary term from the left and drop it on its correct definition on the right. Click the \"Check Me\" button to see if you are correct.    Find the words in the lesson above and try again.     bit  A binary digit, either 0 or 1.    abstraction  The process of removing detail to focus on the essential characteristics of something.    encoding  Converting information into a specific format for storage or transmission.    roundoff error  The error that occurs when a number is approximated to fit in a fixed number of bits.    overflow error  The error that occurs when a number is too large to be represented within the given number of bits.    "
