  "body": "  The following code figures out a ticket price for a movie according to the user's age and the time at which the movie starts. Add a nested if statement to check for whether the movie is playing before 3 PM for a matinee discount. The movie theater opens at 1 PM, so don't worry about AM hours. The variables age and hour have been set for testing, but you can comment out those lines to use your input too.    age = int(input(\"Enter age:\")) hour = int(input(\"Enter PM hour (1-9):\")) # For testing age = 15 hour = 6 if age > 12: # Add a nested if statement to test hour # Set price to 12 if hour is less than 3, else set price to 15 else: price = 10 print(\"Ticket price:\", price, \"dollars.\")  from unittest.gui import TestCaseGui class myTests(TestCaseGui): def test1(self): # remove comments actual = \"\\n\".join( line for line in self.getEditorText().splitlines() if line.strip() and not line.lstrip().startswith(\"#\") ) input_count = actual.count(\"if\") self.assertLessEqual(2,input_count, \"at least 2 if statements\") input_count = actual.count(\"else\") self.assertLessEqual(2,input_count, \"at least 2 else statements\") self.assertIn(\"15\",self.getOutput(),\"Output when age is 15 and hour is 6 should be 15\") myTests().main()   "
